<!--
Ammo Blueprint Tutorial

What is an ammo blueprint?
Ammo blueprints define ammo types for weapons that use ammo. Internally, each combination of
weapon and ammo is a separate weapon, but that gets messy quickly. Ammo blueprints are used to
automatically generate these weapons, using the base weapon and applying new stats defined by
the ammo blueprint.

Starting out
Use <GB_ammoBlueprint name="NAME"> to declare an ammo blueprint. When generating a weapon with
ammo, the name is appended with a leading underscore to the end of the base weapon name. For
example, let's say we have a weapon named "GB_AC_1", and an ammo type named "FLECHETTE". The
generated weapon corresponding to the weapon and ammo combination would be named
"GB_AC_1_FLECHETTE". This is useful to know if you want to use a generated weapon in a list.

continue later
-->

<GB_ammoBlueprint name="CASELESS" ammoType="AUTOCANNON">
	<title>base .. " [Caseless G]"</title>
	<short>base .. " [CL]"</short>
	<cooldown>(2/3) * base</cooldown>
	<freeMissileChance>if(damage >= 3, base - 10, base - 5)</freeMissileChance>
	<weaponArt>base .. "_CASELESS"</weaponArt>
</GB_ammoBlueprint>

<GB_ammoBlueprint name="TEST" ammoType="AUTOCANNON">
	<title>base .. " [Test]"</title>
	<short>base .. " [T]"</short>
	<installReq>Funny</installReq>
	<if>
		<condition>damage == 1</condition>
		<stats>
			<cooldown>0</cooldown>
			<desc>base .. " PEW PEW PEW PEW!"</desc>
		</stats>
	</if>
	<match nameContains="2">
		<breachChance>10</breachChance>
		<sp>10</sp>
		<stun>99</stun>
		<speed>200</speed>
		<description>base .. " The piercer."</description>
	</match>
	<match nameEquals="GB_AC_3">
		<damage>99</damage>
		<cooldown>15</cooldown>
		<description>base .. " Big chonker."</description>
	</match>
	<match hasTag="banana">
		<sp>-100</sp>
	</match>
	<match literalNode="true">Match</match>
</GB_ammoBlueprint>